1
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:05,266
I'm Peppa Pig. [snorts]

2
00:00:05,333 --> 00:00:08,033
-This is my little brother, George.
-[snorts]

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,333
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[Mommy Pig snorts]

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:12,066
And this is Daddy Pig.

5
00:00:12,133 --> 00:00:14,133
-[Daddy Pig snorts]
-[all laugh]

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [snorts]

7
00:00:17,466 --> 00:00:19,766
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:23,500
[narrator] Peppa and her family
are watching sport on television.

9
00:00:26,033 --> 00:00:30,433
It's a long jump. It's a new world record.

10
00:00:30,500 --> 00:00:31,799
[crowd on TV] Hooray!

11
00:00:32,033 --> 00:00:35,233
[snorts] Mommy, what's a world record?

12
00:00:35,300 --> 00:00:38,133
It means you're best
in the world at something.

13
00:00:38,199 --> 00:00:41,366
Then you are a champion
and your name goes in a book.

14
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:46,666
There are champions for running,
jumping, swimming...

15
00:00:46,733 --> 00:00:49,466
I wish you were in the book, Daddy.

16
00:00:49,533 --> 00:00:52,199
-I am in the book.
-No.

17
00:00:52,266 --> 00:00:56,099
Yes, Daddy Pig is champion puddle jumper.

18
00:00:56,166 --> 00:00:57,233
[Peppa &amp; George] Wow.

19
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,066
[Daddy Pig] No one has beaten me yet.

20
00:00:59,133 --> 00:01:01,233
I don't think they ever will.

21
00:01:01,300 --> 00:01:04,666
The next event is the puddle jump.

22
00:01:06,666 --> 00:01:07,700
[crowd cheering on TV]

23
00:01:07,766 --> 00:01:10,166
That was a very big splash.

24
00:01:10,233 --> 00:01:15,500
In fact, I think...
Yes, it's a new world record.

25
00:01:16,133 --> 00:01:17,133
Oh.

26
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:21,300
[snorts] Daddy,
you're not the champion anymore.

27
00:01:21,366 --> 00:01:23,666
Everyone will be sad.

28
00:01:23,733 --> 00:01:25,033
Ho, ho.

29
00:01:25,100 --> 00:01:28,399
I'm sure they've got more important things
to worry about, Peppa.

30
00:01:28,466 --> 00:01:29,566
[doorbell rings]

31
00:01:30,366 --> 00:01:33,033
Daddy Pig, you lost the world record.

32
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:37,133
-Everybody wants you to be champion again.
-It's important.

33
00:01:37,199 --> 00:01:38,199
Really?

34
00:01:38,266 --> 00:01:39,399
[all] Yes.

35
00:01:39,466 --> 00:01:42,300
Okay, I'll do it. Tomorrow.

36
00:01:42,366 --> 00:01:43,533
[crowd] Hooray!

37
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:47,333
But I'll have to train myself
to jump in muddy puddles again.

38
00:01:47,399 --> 00:01:51,233
Everyone knows how
to jump in muddy puddles, Daddy.

39
00:01:51,300 --> 00:01:55,066
Ah, but not everyone is a champion, Peppa.

40
00:01:55,133 --> 00:01:58,466
Daddy Pig is the master.

41
00:01:59,100 --> 00:02:03,000
Daddy, are you going
to practice jumping up and down?

42
00:02:03,066 --> 00:02:07,100
No, Peppa.
I must be at one with the puddle.

43
00:02:07,166 --> 00:02:08,199
What?

44
00:02:08,266 --> 00:02:11,766
To jump in a puddle,
I must think like a puddle.

45
00:02:12,466 --> 00:02:15,266
-Do you need to do running?
-No.

46
00:02:15,333 --> 00:02:17,766
Do you need to do press-ups?

47
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:18,700
No.

48
00:02:19,166 --> 00:02:22,333
I need to sleep. And dream about puddles.

49
00:02:23,100 --> 00:02:24,366
[rooster crows]

50
00:02:24,433 --> 00:02:27,066
[narrator] It is the day
of the big puddle jump.

51
00:02:27,133 --> 00:02:30,566
Daddy Pig is wearing
his puddle-jumping costume.

52
00:02:30,633 --> 00:02:33,400
I can't find my golden boots.

53
00:02:33,466 --> 00:02:36,400
I gave those old boots to Grandpa,
for gardening.

54
00:02:36,466 --> 00:02:41,400
My lucky golden boots?
To be used as gardening boots?

55
00:02:41,466 --> 00:02:44,700
-You've got other ones.
-It's not the same.

56
00:02:44,766 --> 00:02:47,033
[phone ringing]

57
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:48,100
Hello?

58
00:02:48,166 --> 00:02:51,466
Grandpa,
remember those old boots I gave you?

59
00:02:51,533 --> 00:02:53,433
Uh... yes.

60
00:02:53,500 --> 00:02:57,466
Daddy needs them back urgently.
You have been looking after them?

61
00:02:57,533 --> 00:03:00,333
Um, they have been watered.

62
00:03:00,400 --> 00:03:05,066
[narrator] Grandpa Pig is growing tomatoes
in Daddy's lucky boots.

63
00:03:05,600 --> 00:03:08,299
[snorts] We need them
for the puddle jump today.

64
00:03:08,366 --> 00:03:11,266
Right-o. I'll meet you there.

65
00:03:11,333 --> 00:03:12,399
[all chattering]

66
00:03:12,466 --> 00:03:16,500
[narrator] Everyone has come
to watch Daddy Pig's puddle jump.

67
00:03:20,733 --> 00:03:26,266
Please, welcome your friend and mine,
Mr. Potato.

68
00:03:26,333 --> 00:03:28,066
[crowd] Hooray!

69
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:33,466
Good luck, Daddy Pig.
Oh, but where are your lucky boots?

70
00:03:33,533 --> 00:03:35,200
Ah. Here they are.

71
00:03:35,266 --> 00:03:37,200
Thank you, Grandpa Pig.

72
00:03:37,266 --> 00:03:40,100
[sniffs] I can smell tomatoes.

73
00:03:41,100 --> 00:03:44,299
And now for Daddy Pig's puddle jump.

74
00:03:45,366 --> 00:03:47,433
[narrator] Daddy Pig is thinking.

75
00:03:47,500 --> 00:03:49,700
Ready. Steady.

76
00:03:49,766 --> 00:03:51,200
Go.

77
00:03:51,799 --> 00:03:55,333
I must become one with the puddle.

78
00:03:55,399 --> 00:03:57,533
I must be the puddle.

79
00:03:59,166 --> 00:04:01,100
[yells]

80
00:04:03,233 --> 00:04:05,366
The puddle has gone.

81
00:04:05,433 --> 00:04:09,066
[giggles] The puddle has gone
over all of us.

82
00:04:09,133 --> 00:04:12,333
[narrator] Daddy Pig has become one
with the puddle.

83
00:04:12,399 --> 00:04:15,466
Everyone has become one with the puddle.

84
00:04:15,533 --> 00:04:18,666
It's a new world record.

85
00:04:18,733 --> 00:04:20,000
[crowd] Hooray!

86
00:04:20,066 --> 00:04:22,333
[snorts] Champion Daddy Pig.

87
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:24,033
And who is this?

88
00:04:24,099 --> 00:04:25,733
I'm Peppa Pig.

89
00:04:25,800 --> 00:04:30,200
One day,
I will be the champion puddle jumper.

90
00:04:30,266 --> 00:04:31,733
I've been training her.

91
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:34,700
Ah, to be trained by the master.

92
00:04:34,766 --> 00:04:36,400
What have you learned?

93
00:04:36,466 --> 00:04:40,066
Uh... if you jump in muddy puddles,

94
00:04:40,133 --> 00:04:42,800
you must wear your boots.

95
00:04:43,033 --> 00:04:45,033
[crowd laughing]

96
00:04:47,466 --> 00:04:49,033
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

97
00:04:49,099 --> 00:04:51,133
[narrator] It is a lovely sunny day,

98
00:04:51,200 --> 00:04:53,599
and Suzy Sheep has come
to play with Peppa.

99
00:04:53,666 --> 00:04:55,466
[snorts] Hello, Suzy.

100
00:04:55,533 --> 00:04:57,533
[bleats] Hello, Peppa.

101
00:04:57,599 --> 00:05:00,099
[narrator] Peppa and Suzy
are best friends.

102
00:05:00,166 --> 00:05:02,366
Guess what happened to me yesterday.

103
00:05:02,433 --> 00:05:06,566
[snorts] Yesterday I went to the duck pond
and I saw Mrs. Duck.

104
00:05:06,633 --> 00:05:07,700
Well, yesterday--

105
00:05:07,766 --> 00:05:10,766
Then I went to the supermarket with Mommy.

106
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,200
We bought bread, carrots and...

107
00:05:13,700 --> 00:05:14,766
What's wrong?

108
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:16,566
You talk too much.

109
00:05:16,633 --> 00:05:19,233
You go, "Blah, blah, blah."

110
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:22,200
Just like that, "Blah, blah, blah."

111
00:05:23,133 --> 00:05:26,000
Mummy, Suzy said I talk too much.

112
00:05:26,066 --> 00:05:29,233
Well, you are a bit of a chatterbox,
Peppa.

113
00:05:29,300 --> 00:05:31,366
Chatterbox. That's right.

114
00:05:31,433 --> 00:05:34,233
Chatterbox here. Chatterbox there.

115
00:05:34,700 --> 00:05:38,500
Chatter, chatter, chatter.
You never stop talking.

116
00:05:38,566 --> 00:05:42,599
[snorts] I can easily stop talking
if I want to.

117
00:05:42,666 --> 00:05:44,000
No, you can't.

118
00:05:44,066 --> 00:05:45,433
Yes, I can.

119
00:05:45,500 --> 00:05:46,633
You can't.

120
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:48,333
I can.

121
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:49,666
You can't.

122
00:05:49,733 --> 00:05:51,200
That's it.

123
00:05:51,266 --> 00:05:53,666
I'm never going to talk again.

124
00:05:54,466 --> 00:05:55,366
[bell dings]

125
00:05:55,433 --> 00:05:57,800
Hello, Suzy. Hello, Peppa.

126
00:05:58,033 --> 00:06:01,333
[bleats] Hello, Zoë. You look nice today.

127
00:06:01,400 --> 00:06:05,533
Thank you, Suzy. This is my new dress.

128
00:06:06,566 --> 00:06:09,200
Why are you not talking, Peppa?

129
00:06:09,266 --> 00:06:12,200
Yes. Why are you not talking, Peppa?

130
00:06:12,266 --> 00:06:14,599
[sighs] This is a silly game.

131
00:06:14,666 --> 00:06:16,500
What game are you playing?

132
00:06:16,566 --> 00:06:20,733
Suzy said I was a chatterbox
and I could never be quiet.

133
00:06:20,799 --> 00:06:24,633
You're not being very quiet now,
are you? [laughs]

134
00:06:24,700 --> 00:06:28,366
Right. I'm not going to talk ever again.

135
00:06:28,433 --> 00:06:30,766
Starting now.

136
00:06:31,533 --> 00:06:32,500
[bell dings]

137
00:06:32,566 --> 00:06:34,099
Hello, everyone.

138
00:06:34,166 --> 00:06:35,266
Hello, Danny.

139
00:06:35,333 --> 00:06:36,500
Hello, Danny.

140
00:06:37,166 --> 00:06:39,066
What's the matter with Peppa?

141
00:06:39,133 --> 00:06:41,133
She's not talking.

142
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:43,766
Oh. Who wants a grape?

143
00:06:44,000 --> 00:06:44,799
Me, please.

144
00:06:45,033 --> 00:06:46,099
Me, please.

145
00:06:46,166 --> 00:06:47,666
[grunts]

146
00:06:47,733 --> 00:06:51,366
You can't nod your head. That's cheating.

147
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:53,500
And you can't blink.

148
00:06:54,200 --> 00:06:55,133
[horn honks]

149
00:06:55,200 --> 00:06:56,400
Hello, everyone.

150
00:06:56,466 --> 00:06:58,266
[all] Hello, Pedro.

151
00:06:58,333 --> 00:07:00,433
What's the matter with Peppa?

152
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:03,433
She's never going to talk ever again.

153
00:07:03,500 --> 00:07:04,366
Why?

154
00:07:04,433 --> 00:07:06,500
Because she talks too much.

155
00:07:06,566 --> 00:07:09,099
I do not talk too much.

156
00:07:09,166 --> 00:07:12,133
Anyway, you're always walking like this:

157
00:07:12,200 --> 00:07:16,400
"Oh, look at me. I'm Suzy Sheep."

158
00:07:16,466 --> 00:07:18,066
See what I mean?

159
00:07:18,133 --> 00:07:19,766
And you say this:

160
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:22,333
Micky macky boo bah boo.

161
00:07:22,400 --> 00:07:24,233
That's nothing like me.

162
00:07:24,299 --> 00:07:27,033
It is a bit like you, Suzy.

163
00:07:27,099 --> 00:07:30,000
You're just as noisy as me. [snorts]

164
00:07:30,066 --> 00:07:31,666
I can be quiet.

165
00:07:31,733 --> 00:07:33,500
It's not easy.

166
00:07:33,566 --> 00:07:36,033
It's not that hard, Peppa.

167
00:07:36,099 --> 00:07:38,266
Okay. You do it, then.

168
00:07:38,333 --> 00:07:40,299
Let's all do it.

169
00:07:40,366 --> 00:07:42,166
We can show my mommy.

170
00:07:42,233 --> 00:07:44,233
[all giggling]

171
00:07:46,000 --> 00:07:48,266
Mommy, we're all going to be quiet.

172
00:07:48,333 --> 00:07:50,099
Very quiet.

173
00:07:50,166 --> 00:07:54,500
So quiet you can drop something
on the floor and hear it.

174
00:07:54,566 --> 00:07:56,166
Quiet as a mouse.

175
00:07:56,233 --> 00:07:57,433
[all giggle]

176
00:07:58,066 --> 00:08:01,733
But you're not being quiet at all.
You're all being very noisy.

177
00:08:01,799 --> 00:08:05,299
We can be quiet whenever we want.

178
00:08:05,366 --> 00:08:08,500
Start being quiet on the count of three.

179
00:08:08,566 --> 00:08:11,200
-One, two--
-I'm not ready.

180
00:08:11,266 --> 00:08:12,666
Okay, now.

181
00:08:12,733 --> 00:08:13,599
On your marks.

182
00:08:13,666 --> 00:08:15,133
-Ready...
-Get set.

183
00:08:15,200 --> 00:08:16,066
Three.

184
00:08:16,533 --> 00:08:17,700
[horn honks]

185
00:08:17,766 --> 00:08:20,299
Hello. [snorts] I'm home.

186
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:24,500
Oh. I thought the house was empty.

187
00:08:24,566 --> 00:08:27,666
Peppa and her friends are playing
at being quiet.

188
00:08:27,733 --> 00:08:31,266
[snorts] It's not playing.
It's very hard work.

189
00:08:31,333 --> 00:08:33,199
[children] Oh, Peppa.

190
00:08:33,266 --> 00:08:36,100
[narrator] Peppa cannot stop herself
from talking.

191
00:08:36,166 --> 00:08:37,633
Oh, Daddy.

192
00:08:37,699 --> 00:08:40,500
I think I might be a chatterbox.

193
00:08:40,566 --> 00:08:43,500
That's not such a bad thing, Peppa.

194
00:08:43,566 --> 00:08:45,066
It's good to talk.

195
00:08:45,133 --> 00:08:48,333
In fact,
I think you're an expert at talking.

196
00:08:48,400 --> 00:08:50,100
That's right. [snorts]

197
00:08:50,166 --> 00:08:52,766
I am an expert at talking.

198
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,666
[bleats] I'm an expert at talking, too.

199
00:08:55,733 --> 00:08:58,800
No, you're not. I'm the chatterbox.

200
00:08:59,033 --> 00:09:01,433
I'm more of a chatterbox than you.

201
00:09:01,500 --> 00:09:02,533
Ho, ho.

202
00:09:02,600 --> 00:09:04,300
You two are just the same.

203
00:09:04,366 --> 00:09:05,766
Yes, we are.

204
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:09,366
-That's why we are best friends.
-Chatter, chatter...

205
00:09:09,433 --> 00:09:13,366
[narrator] Peppa loves talking.
Suzy loves talking.

206
00:09:13,433 --> 00:09:15,733
Everybody loves talking.

207
00:09:15,800 --> 00:09:16,766
[all] Chatter...

208
00:09:19,033 --> 00:09:21,166
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

209
00:09:22,033 --> 00:09:26,199
[narrator] It is a lovely sunny day.
Peppa is playing with her friends.

210
00:09:26,266 --> 00:09:28,666
[snorts] It's Freddy Fox.

211
00:09:31,800 --> 00:09:33,766
[barks] Hello, everyone.

212
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,600
-[all] Hello, Freddy.
-[Freddy barks]

213
00:09:35,666 --> 00:09:38,633
Come on, let's cycle to the big hill.

214
00:09:38,699 --> 00:09:40,566
[all cheer, then giggle]

215
00:09:41,199 --> 00:09:42,600
Good morning, Mr. Fox.

216
00:09:42,666 --> 00:09:44,500
It's afternoon, Mr. Pig.

217
00:09:44,566 --> 00:09:48,433
Afternoon? Already?
My watch must have stopped.

218
00:09:48,500 --> 00:09:53,366
My shop sells watches and clocks.
Let me see what I've got in the van.

219
00:09:55,199 --> 00:09:56,800
One grandfather clock.

220
00:09:57,033 --> 00:09:58,466
It's a bit big.

221
00:09:58,533 --> 00:09:59,533
Good, isn't it?

222
00:09:59,600 --> 00:10:02,199
It actually comes in a set of three.

223
00:10:02,266 --> 00:10:03,233
Oh.

224
00:10:03,300 --> 00:10:05,300
[bells dinging]

225
00:10:07,166 --> 00:10:09,500
[snorts] Who's got the loudest bell?

226
00:10:09,566 --> 00:10:12,000
[bells dinging]

227
00:10:12,066 --> 00:10:13,633
I haven't got a bell.

228
00:10:13,699 --> 00:10:14,566
Oh.

229
00:10:14,633 --> 00:10:17,766
But my dad will have one
in the back of his van.

230
00:10:20,666 --> 00:10:23,733
-Three clocks are much better than one.
-Dad?

231
00:10:23,800 --> 00:10:26,300
Have you got a bicycle bell, please?

232
00:10:26,366 --> 00:10:28,033
How many do you want, son?

233
00:10:28,100 --> 00:10:29,699
I only want one.

234
00:10:29,766 --> 00:10:31,733
I do them in boxes of two.

235
00:10:32,466 --> 00:10:35,433
[narrator] Freddy Fox
now has two bicycle bells.

236
00:10:35,500 --> 00:10:36,633
[bells dinging]

237
00:10:36,699 --> 00:10:37,766
Brilliant.

238
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:39,400
Thanks, Dad.

239
00:10:39,466 --> 00:10:41,466
[bells dinging]

240
00:10:42,166 --> 00:10:44,400
Dad gave me two bells.

241
00:10:44,800 --> 00:10:46,033
[all] Wow.

242
00:10:46,100 --> 00:10:48,766
What else has your dad got in his van?

243
00:10:49,000 --> 00:10:51,466
He's got everything.

244
00:10:51,533 --> 00:10:53,133
[all] Ooh.

245
00:10:53,199 --> 00:10:55,533
[snorts] What shall we play now?

246
00:10:55,600 --> 00:10:58,199
Let's have a bicycle race.

247
00:10:58,266 --> 00:11:01,800
With a big shiny cup for the winner.

248
00:11:02,033 --> 00:11:04,400
But where can we get a cup?

249
00:11:04,466 --> 00:11:07,566
Yes, where can we get a cup?

250
00:11:08,433 --> 00:11:10,699
I'll see what I can do.

251
00:11:11,699 --> 00:11:15,066
The best thing about having
your own cement mixer is--

252
00:11:15,133 --> 00:11:20,300
Dad, have you got a big shiny winner's cup
for our bicycle race, please?

253
00:11:20,366 --> 00:11:22,800
How important a race is it?

254
00:11:23,033 --> 00:11:25,633
It's very important.

255
00:11:26,699 --> 00:11:28,066
Will this do?

256
00:11:28,133 --> 00:11:31,600
Wow, thanks, Dad. It's gold.

257
00:11:31,666 --> 00:11:34,300
Yes. It's plastic gold.

258
00:11:34,366 --> 00:11:35,500
[Freddy &amp; Daddy Pig] Ooh.

259
00:11:35,566 --> 00:11:38,000
[bells dinging]

260
00:11:38,066 --> 00:11:42,400
One winner's cup.
It's made of plastic gold.

261
00:11:42,466 --> 00:11:43,500
[all] Wow.

262
00:11:43,566 --> 00:11:47,600
Your daddy's van
really has got everything.

263
00:11:47,666 --> 00:11:48,633
Yep.

264
00:11:48,699 --> 00:11:51,566
[neighs] Let's race to Peppa's house.

265
00:11:51,633 --> 00:11:54,100
Ready. Steady. Go.

266
00:11:54,166 --> 00:11:56,166
[bells dinging &amp; children giggling]

267
00:11:58,500 --> 00:12:01,766
Press this button and it just disappears.

268
00:12:02,300 --> 00:12:03,533
[Mommy Pig &amp; Daddy Pig] Ooh.

269
00:12:04,166 --> 00:12:05,400
[Mommy Pig &amp; Daddy Pig] Ah!

270
00:12:05,466 --> 00:12:09,066
And if you push this button,
you can play CDs.

271
00:12:09,133 --> 00:12:10,666
[rock music playing over speakers]

272
00:12:10,733 --> 00:12:12,133
[all giggling]

273
00:12:13,199 --> 00:12:16,233
[narrator] The friends have all finished
together.

274
00:12:16,300 --> 00:12:18,500
-Everyone's a winner.
-[children giggling]

275
00:12:18,566 --> 00:12:21,066
But we've only got one cup.

276
00:12:22,133 --> 00:12:25,199
My van has a winner's cup for everyone.

277
00:12:25,266 --> 00:12:26,266
[both] Hooray!

278
00:12:27,800 --> 00:12:32,466
Mr. Fox, is there anything
you don't have in your van?

279
00:12:32,533 --> 00:12:33,433
Try me.

280
00:12:33,500 --> 00:12:35,566
Have you got a banjo?

281
00:12:36,533 --> 00:12:37,800
Four- or five-string?

282
00:12:38,033 --> 00:12:41,766
[bleats] You won't have a tree
in your van.

283
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,033
-[children giggle]
-Apple or pear?

284
00:12:44,099 --> 00:12:47,766
[woofs] I bet you haven't got a rocket
in there.

285
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:49,033
Boxes of five.

286
00:12:49,099 --> 00:12:51,099
What about a chicken?

287
00:12:51,166 --> 00:12:52,400
One chicken.

288
00:12:52,466 --> 00:12:53,633
[chicken clucks]

289
00:12:53,699 --> 00:12:54,599
[both giggle]

290
00:12:54,666 --> 00:12:57,199
Mr. Fox's van is magic.

291
00:12:57,266 --> 00:12:59,266
It's a super van.

292
00:12:59,333 --> 00:13:02,366
Yes, it is. Come on, Freddy.
We'd better get home.

293
00:13:02,433 --> 00:13:03,800
-Goodbye, everyone.
-Bye.

294
00:13:04,033 --> 00:13:04,800
[all] Bye.

295
00:13:05,033 --> 00:13:07,733
-Have you got a bouncy castle?
-Yep.

296
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:12,133
-A garden shed?
-Yep. I've got everything.

297
00:13:12,199 --> 00:13:14,233
[engine stutters]

298
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,466
Oh, I've got no petrol.

299
00:13:17,233 --> 00:13:21,366
[narrator] Mr. Fox has everything
in his van, except petrol.

300
00:13:21,433 --> 00:13:24,766
Hmm. I need to get to the petrol station.

301
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:27,800
I would tow you,
but I haven't got a towrope.

302
00:13:28,033 --> 00:13:31,766
Oh, I've got plenty of them.
I do them in packs of five.

303
00:13:33,433 --> 00:13:35,099
Can we come along, too?

304
00:13:35,166 --> 00:13:36,566
[chuckles] Why not?

305
00:13:36,633 --> 00:13:38,633
[children giggling]

306
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:43,766
[narrator] Daddy Pig is towing
Mr. Fox's van to the petrol station.

307
00:13:44,000 --> 00:13:46,000
[all laughing]

308
00:13:50,000 --> 00:13:52,133
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

309
00:13:52,199 --> 00:13:55,766
[narrator] Peppa and her family
are on their way to visit Cousin Chloé.

310
00:13:56,000 --> 00:13:59,066
I love playing with big Cousin Chloé.

311
00:13:59,133 --> 00:14:01,133
[George snorts, then both giggle]

312
00:14:02,466 --> 00:14:04,433
-[snorts] Chloé! Chloé!
-Chloé! Chloé!

313
00:14:04,500 --> 00:14:07,000
-Oh. Chloé.
-Hi there.

314
00:14:07,066 --> 00:14:11,333
These are my friends
Simon Squirrel and Belinda Bear.

315
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,400
You can call me Si. It's short for Simon.

316
00:14:14,466 --> 00:14:18,300
And I'm Bee. It's short for Belinda.

317
00:14:18,366 --> 00:14:19,733
[snorts] I'm Peppa.

318
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:22,466
-We'll call you Peh.
-Oh.

319
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:25,066
And this is George.

320
00:14:25,133 --> 00:14:27,633
-We'll call you Ger.
-Oh.

321
00:14:27,699 --> 00:14:31,199
You didn't tell us you had baby cousins,
Chloé.

322
00:14:31,266 --> 00:14:33,566
[snorts] I'm not a baby.

323
00:14:33,633 --> 00:14:35,433
But you're both little.

324
00:14:35,500 --> 00:14:37,300
I'm a big girl.

325
00:14:37,366 --> 00:14:39,166
George is little.

326
00:14:39,233 --> 00:14:41,666
Uh... why don't we all play a game?

327
00:14:41,733 --> 00:14:45,066
-[snorts] Yes. Let's play hide-and-seek.
-[snorts]

328
00:14:45,533 --> 00:14:48,433
We don't play baby games anymore.

329
00:14:48,500 --> 00:14:50,366
We're almost grown up.

330
00:14:50,800 --> 00:14:53,466
[snorts] What about the yes-no game?

331
00:14:53,533 --> 00:14:55,699
What's the yes-no game?

332
00:14:55,766 --> 00:14:59,166
I ask things and you answer.

333
00:14:59,233 --> 00:15:01,566
What makes that a game?

334
00:15:01,633 --> 00:15:04,599
You mustn't say yes or no.

335
00:15:04,666 --> 00:15:06,099
Too easy.

336
00:15:06,166 --> 00:15:08,500
-Do you want to play, then?
-Yes.

337
00:15:08,566 --> 00:15:10,366
Aha! You said yes.

338
00:15:10,433 --> 00:15:11,500
[Peppa &amp; George giggle]

339
00:15:11,566 --> 00:15:14,000
That's not fair. I wasn't ready.

340
00:15:14,066 --> 00:15:16,166
Bee? Are you ready?

341
00:15:16,233 --> 00:15:17,199
Yes.

342
00:15:17,266 --> 00:15:19,400
Aha! I win again. [giggling]

343
00:15:19,466 --> 00:15:22,366
[narrator] Peppa is very good
at playing the yes-no game.

344
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:25,133
Can I ask the questions?

345
00:15:25,199 --> 00:15:26,233
Of course.

346
00:15:26,300 --> 00:15:29,533
You don't mind me
asking you the questions?

347
00:15:29,599 --> 00:15:31,466
I don't mind.

348
00:15:31,533 --> 00:15:34,400
Am I ever going to make you say yes or no?

349
00:15:34,466 --> 00:15:36,066
I don't think so.

350
00:15:36,133 --> 00:15:37,599
Oh, I give up.

351
00:15:37,666 --> 00:15:40,133
How do you always win?

352
00:15:40,199 --> 00:15:44,033
Easy. I just don't say yes or no.

353
00:15:44,099 --> 00:15:47,033
Ah! I win. You said yes and no.

354
00:15:47,099 --> 00:15:48,066
[all laugh]

355
00:15:48,133 --> 00:15:49,199
That was fun.

356
00:15:49,266 --> 00:15:51,099
Let's play another game.

357
00:15:51,166 --> 00:15:53,533
Have you ever played sardines?

358
00:15:53,599 --> 00:15:55,000
What's that?

359
00:15:55,066 --> 00:15:58,333
Someone hides and we all try to find them.

360
00:15:58,400 --> 00:16:01,066
That sounds like hide-and-seek.

361
00:16:01,133 --> 00:16:04,166
But when you find them, you keep quiet

362
00:16:04,233 --> 00:16:06,033
and hide in the same space.

363
00:16:06,099 --> 00:16:08,033
Until everyone is hiding there.

364
00:16:08,099 --> 00:16:10,733
Like sardines in a tin.

365
00:16:10,800 --> 00:16:13,233
All right. Let's try it.

366
00:16:13,300 --> 00:16:16,666
-[George snorts]
-George, you hide first.

367
00:16:16,733 --> 00:16:17,666
[George giggles]

368
00:16:17,733 --> 00:16:21,066
[all] One, two, three...

369
00:16:21,133 --> 00:16:24,099
[narrator] George is looking
for somewhere to hide.

370
00:16:24,166 --> 00:16:26,033
[all] ...nine, ten.

371
00:16:26,099 --> 00:16:28,733
Ready or not, here we come.

372
00:16:28,800 --> 00:16:30,366
-[George giggles]
-[Peppa snorts]

373
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:34,300
George, I can see your wiggly tail.
[giggles]

374
00:16:34,366 --> 00:16:36,266
[narrator] Peppa is hiding with George.

375
00:16:36,333 --> 00:16:38,500
[Peppa whispering] Move over, George.

376
00:16:38,566 --> 00:16:39,533
Found you.

377
00:16:39,599 --> 00:16:43,233
[narrator] Now Chloé must squeeze in
with Peppa and George.

378
00:16:43,300 --> 00:16:44,800
-[Peppa giggles]
-[Chloé] Move up.

379
00:16:45,400 --> 00:16:47,433
There you all are.

380
00:16:47,500 --> 00:16:50,366
[narrator] Now Belinda Bear
must squeeze in, too.

381
00:16:50,433 --> 00:16:52,099
-[Belinda] Budge up.
-[Peppa snorts]

382
00:16:52,166 --> 00:16:54,699
We're like sardines in a tin. [giggles]

383
00:16:56,333 --> 00:16:58,066
Where's everyone gone?

384
00:16:58,133 --> 00:16:59,166
[all] Surprise!

385
00:16:59,233 --> 00:17:00,166
[Simon yells]

386
00:17:00,233 --> 00:17:01,599
[all laugh]

387
00:17:01,666 --> 00:17:03,766
Can we stop running around now?

388
00:17:04,000 --> 00:17:07,099
Yeah, let's just chill out.

389
00:17:07,166 --> 00:17:10,200
Chill out? What's that?

390
00:17:10,266 --> 00:17:13,099
We just sit around and talk about stuff.

391
00:17:13,166 --> 00:17:16,599
[snorts] I like talking. Blah, blah, blah.

392
00:17:16,666 --> 00:17:19,133
Let's talk about music.

393
00:17:19,200 --> 00:17:21,533
I dig blues music.

394
00:17:21,599 --> 00:17:24,466
Um... I like reds music.

395
00:17:24,533 --> 00:17:26,633
I like greens music.

396
00:17:26,700 --> 00:17:29,600
We don't like children's music.

397
00:17:29,666 --> 00:17:31,366
[older children] No, no, no.

398
00:17:31,433 --> 00:17:33,733
What music are you into?

399
00:17:33,800 --> 00:17:37,666
I like this. It's very grown-up.

400
00:17:38,166 --> 00:17:41,766
♪ Heads, shoulders, knees and toes
Knees and toes ♪

401
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:45,200
♪ Heads, shoulders, knees and toes
Knees and toes ♪

402
00:17:45,266 --> 00:17:49,033
♪ And eyes and ears and mouth and nose ♪

403
00:17:49,100 --> 00:17:52,533
♪ Heads, shoulders, knees and toes
Knees and toes ♪

404
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:54,433
♪ Heads, shoulders, knees and toes... ♪

405
00:17:54,500 --> 00:17:56,466
[snorts] Peppa. George.

406
00:17:56,533 --> 00:17:58,166
It's time to go home now.

407
00:17:58,233 --> 00:17:59,533
-[music stops]
-[children] Aw.

408
00:17:59,600 --> 00:18:01,266
You will see Chloé again soon.

409
00:18:01,333 --> 00:18:04,333
I'm coming to your house next week, Peppa.

410
00:18:04,399 --> 00:18:06,066
[both] Can we come along, too?

411
00:18:06,133 --> 00:18:09,133
You can come,
but we will be playing games.

412
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:12,333
We like playing games
with Peppa and George.

413
00:18:12,399 --> 00:18:13,500
[piglets] Hooray!

414
00:18:13,566 --> 00:18:16,266
[narrator] You can still have fun
playing games,

415
00:18:16,333 --> 00:18:18,466
even when you're almost grown up.

416
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:22,533
♪ Heads, shoulders, knees and toes
Knees and toes ♪

417
00:18:22,600 --> 00:18:25,633
♪ Heads, shoulders, knees and toes
Knees and toes ♪

418
00:18:25,700 --> 00:18:29,800
♪ And eyes and ears and mouth and nose ♪

419
00:18:30,033 --> 00:18:33,600
♪ Heads, shoulders, knees and toes
Knees and toes ♪

